  {
   "id": "ex1",
   "type": "example",
   "problem": {
    "en": "Compute the crude and standardised death rates of towns A and B and say which is healthier. Age groups 0–15, 15–50, 50+. Town A: population 2,000, 6,000, 2,000, SDR 12, 5, 40. Town B: population 4,000, 5,000, 1,000, SDR 10, 6, 45. Standard population 3,000, 5,000, 2,000."
   },
   "steps": [
    {
     "en": "Deaths in A = 24 + 30 + 80 = 134; CDR(A) = 134/10,000 × 1000 = 13.4."
    },
    {
     "en": "Deaths in B = 40 + 30 + 45 = 115; CDR(B) = 11.5."
    },
    {
     "en": "STDR(A) = 1,41,000/10,000 = 14.1; STDR(B) = 1,50,000/10,000 = 15.0."
    },
    {
     "en": "STDR(A) < STDR(B), so town A is healthier, although its CDR is higher."
    }
   ],
   "answer": {
    "en": "CDR: A 13.4, B 11.5; STDR: A 14.1, B 15.0; A is healthier"
   },
